From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "sh.chao" <sh.chao@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Veloce r25-3-0104: add sparse exact native sidecars

Keep canonical PDFium as the zero-retained-state holder path. Start the
parser-time builder lazily at the first path ordinal, ignore non-path
objects, and return no RenderProgram when no exact native command was
lowered.

Replace the copied one-byte-per-object stream with bounded homogeneous
native runs. Source-ordinal gaps are implicit canonical spans, preserving
painter order without bounds, bytecode, or retained metadata for canonical
objects. Validate immutable run and index structure once when sealing the
sidecar.

Use contiguous line leaves as allocation-free spatial skip units and retain
command blocks only for owned path runs. This avoids one block per canonical
gap on CAD pages while keeping bounded culling for both line- and path-heavy
holders. Fall back to the canonical object if a replay matrix is unavailable.
